<quiz>
<question type="stack">
  <name><text>Mean from a frequency table</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>The table shows [[if test="is(a=0)"]]the number of goals scored in each match of a county football league season[[elif test="is(a=1)"]]the number of people in each household in a village near Kitui[[else]]the number of eggs collected each day from a small poultry unit[[/if]].</p><table border="1" style="border-collapse:collapse;text-align:center;"><tr><th style="padding:4px 10px;">[[if test="is(a=0)"]]Goals[[elif test="is(a=1)"]]People[[else]]Eggs[[/if]] (\(x\))</th><th style="padding:4px 10px;">{@xv[1]@}</th><th style="padding:4px 10px;">{@xv[2]@}</th><th style="padding:4px 10px;">{@xv[3]@}</th><th style="padding:4px 10px;">{@xv[4]@}</th><th style="padding:4px 10px;">{@xv[5]@}</th><th style="padding:4px 10px;">{@xv[6]@}</th></tr><tr><td style="padding:4px 10px;">Frequency (\(f\))</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@f[1]@}</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@f[2]@}</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@f[3]@}</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@f[4]@}</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@f[5]@}</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@f[6]@}</td></tr></table><p>(a) Find \(\Sigma f\).</p><div>\(\Sigma f =\) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div><p>(b) Find \(\Sigma fx\).</p><div>\(\Sigma fx =\) [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div><p>(c) Find the mean, correct to 1 decimal place.</p><div>\(\bar{x} =\) [[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</div>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>A frequency table is a short way of listing repeated values: the value \(x\) occurs \(f\) times. The mean uses every value, weighted by its frequency, so multiply each \(x\) by its frequency, add these products, and divide by the total frequency.</p><table border="1" style="border-collapse:collapse;text-align:center;"><tr><th style="padding:4px 10px;">\(x\)</th><th style="padding:4px 10px;">{@xv[1]@}</th><th style="padding:4px 10px;">{@xv[2]@}</th><th style="padding:4px 10px;">{@xv[3]@}</th><th style="padding:4px 10px;">{@xv[4]@}</th><th style="padding:4px 10px;">{@xv[5]@}</th><th style="padding:4px 10px;">{@xv[6]@}</th><th style="padding:4px 10px;">Total</th></tr><tr><td style="padding:4px 10px;">\(f\)</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@f[1]@}</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@f[2]@}</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@f[3]@}</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@f[4]@}</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@f[5]@}</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@f[6]@}</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@n@}</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:4px 10px;">\(fx\)</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@f[1]*xv[1]@}</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@f[2]*xv[2]@}</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@f[3]*xv[3]@}</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@f[4]*xv[4]@}</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@f[5]*xv[5]@}</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@f[6]*xv[6]@}</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@Sfx@}</td></tr></table><p>(a) \(\Sigma f = {@n@}\). (b) \(\Sigma fx = {@Sfx@}\).</p><p>(c) \[\bar{x} = \frac{\Sigma fx}{\Sigma f} = \frac{ {@Sfx@} }{ {@n@} } \approx {@mnd@}\]</p>]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
  <defaultgrade>3</defaultgrade>
  <penalty>0.1</penalty>
  <hidden>0</hidden>
  <idnumber></idnumber>
  <stackversion><text>2026063000</text></stackversion>
  <questionvariables>
    <text><![CDATA[/* exd: shortest exact decimal display of a terminating value (up to 3 d.p.) */
exd(v) := if integerp(v) then v else if integerp(10*v) then dispdp(float(v),1) else if integerp(100*v) then dispdp(float(v),2) else dispdp(float(v),3);
/* Design: mean from a frequency table. Source: original. */
flist: [[2,2,7,10,11,4],[1,2,4,9,13,9],[3,5,6,7,8,12],[1,6,6,14,11,3],[4,5,6,9,12,3],[4,6,5,5,5,3],[6,9,7,6,4,4],[5,9,9,12,4,4],[1,4,4,12,13,9],[1,1,11,12,11,9]];
ix: 1+rand(10);
f: flist[ix];
a: rand(3);
xv: makelist(a+k-1,k,1,6);
n: apply("+",f);
Sfx: sum(f[k]*xv[k],k,1,6);
mn: Sfx/n;
mnd: dispdp(float(floor(10^1*(mn)+1/2)/10^1),1);
/* diagnostics */
Sx: apply("+",xv);
byrows: Sfx/6;
meanx: Sx/6;
meanf: n/6;
/* test values */
mn1: float(floor(10^1*(mn)+1/2)/10^1);
byrows1: float(floor(10^1*(byrows)+1/2)/10^1);
meanx1: float(floor(10^1*(meanx)+1/2)/10^1);
meanf1: float(floor(10^1*(meanf)+1/2)/10^1);
Sfxm: Sfx-2*n;
ft1: float(floor(10^1*((Sfx-2*n)/n)+1/2)/10^1);]]></text>
  </questionvariables>
